The quintessential taste of Southern comfort: classic rolled flat pastry dumplings simmered in rich chicken broth until tender and chewy, releasing just enough flour into the simmering broth to create an ultra-velvety gravy. Paired with juicy, tender shredded chicken, this one-pot dish rivals the beloved roadside original.

*Adapted from [Delish](https://www.delish.com/cooking/recipe-ideas/a40253074/cracker-barrel-chicken-and-dumplings-copycat-recipe/).*

## Ingredients

### Poached Chicken & Broth
- 4 cups low-sodium chicken broth
- 2 cups water
- ½ teaspoon onion powder
- ½ teaspoon kosher salt (plus extra to taste)
- ¼ teaspoon freshly cracked black pepper (plus extra for finishing)
- 2 boneless, skinless chicken breasts (approx. 1 lb total)

### Rolled Dumplings
- 2 cups plus 1 tablespoon all-purpose flour, divided
- ½ teaspoon baking powder
- 1 teaspoon kosher salt
- ¼ cup vegetable shortening, cold
- ¾ cup cold whole buttermilk

## Instructions

1. **Simmer and Poach the Chicken:** In a large Dutch oven or heavy-bottomed stockpot, bring the chicken broth, water, onion powder, ½ teaspoon kosher salt, and a pinch of black pepper to a gentle boil over medium-high heat. Submerge the chicken breasts, reduce heat to medium-low, and cover tightly. Let simmer gently for 12 to 15 minutes, or until the chicken reaches 165°F (74°C) internally. Transfer the chicken breasts to a cutting board or plate to cool.
2. **Mix the Dumpling Dough:** While the chicken poaches, prepare the dumplings. In a medium mixing bowl, whisk together 2 cups of all-purpose flour, the baking powder, and 1 teaspoon of kosher salt. Drop in the cold vegetable shortening and work it into the dry mixture with your fingertips or a pastry cutter until the fat resembles coarse pea-sized crumbs.
3. **Incorporate Buttermilk:** Pour the cold buttermilk into the bowl. Stir with a fork or wooden spoon just until a rough, shaggy dough pulls together.
4. **Knead, Roll, and Cut:** Turn the dough out onto a lightly floured surface. Knead gently about 12 to 15 times until the dough becomes cohesive and smooth. Using a floured rolling pin, roll the dough out evenly to ¼-inch thickness. Slice into approximately 2-inch squares using a chef's knife or pizza wheel (irregular scrap pieces are welcome!). Lightly toss and dust the cut dumplings with the remaining 1 tablespoon of flour to keep them separate.
5. **Boil and Simmer Dumplings:** Turn the burner back up to high and bring the poaching broth to a vigorous rolling boil. Drop the dumplings in individually, giving the pot an occasional gentle stir so they do not clump together. Boil uncovered for 5 minutes.
6. **Simmer to a Rich Gravy:** Lower the heat to medium-low so the broth settles into a steady simmer. Partially cover the pot with the lid slightly askew to allow a little steam to escape. Simmer for about 20 minutes, stirring gently every 5 minutes. The starch dusting the dumplings will naturally thicken the broth into a rich, silky gravy.
7. **Shred Chicken and Assemble:** While the dumplings simmer, shred the rested chicken breasts into bite-sized shreds using two forks. When the dumplings are cooked through and tender, fold the shredded chicken back into the pot. Simmer for 1 to 2 minutes until the chicken is hot.
8. **Season and Serve:** Taste the gravy and adjust with additional kosher salt and a generous grind of black pepper. Ladle steaming bowls immediately.

## Notes

- **Fluffy vs. Flat Dumplings:** Traditional Cracker Barrel dumplings are flat rolled dumplings (essentially fresh Southern eggless pasta), which produce a firm, chewy bite and a thick starchy gravy. Avoid rolling them thicker than ¼ inch so they cook through evenly.
- **Leftover or Rotisserie Chicken:** If using leftover cooked chicken or store-bought rotisserie chicken, skip poaching and jump straight to simmering the broth with onion powder and salt, adding the shredded chicken during the final 2 minutes.
